// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO14 - dedicated onboard 8x8 LED matrix panel
// data line (WS_MATRIX_DIN, see vendor comment "Onboard 8 x 8 Matrix
// panel"). Excludes GPIO10/13 - dedicated onboard QMI8658 IMU interrupt
// lines (WS_IMU_INT1/INT2, see vendor comment "Onboard QMI8658 IMU").
// GPIO11/12 (SDA/SCL) stay available - the vendor's own comment
// "Def for I2C that shares the IMU I2C pins" confirms this is a shared,
// not dedicated, bus.
// pfodWeb NOTE (independent verification, 2026-07-14): confirmed against
// real external vendor sources beyond this repo's own pins_arduino.h -
//   - Waveshare's official wiki page for this exact board
//     (waveshare.com/wiki/ESP32-S3-Matrix) includes an official Arduino
//     "BlinkRGB" example with the line "#define PIN_NEOPIXEL 14",
//     independently corroborating GPIO14 as the onboard 8x8 RGB matrix
//     data line (matches the vendor pins_arduino.h WS_MATRIX_DIN=14
//     macro).
//   - CNX Software's board-launch article (cnx-software.com) and
//     ESPHome's device page (devices.esphome.io/devices/
//     waveshare-esp32s3-matrix/) independently describe the onboard
//     QMI8658 IMU using GPIO10 as an interrupt pin and the 8x8 RGB matrix
//     on GPIO14, corroborating the vendor pins_arduino.h WS_IMU_INT1/
//     WS_MATRIX_DIN assignments.
// GPIO13 (WS_IMU_INT2) and the shared-I2C reasoning for GPIO11/12 were not
// independently corroborated beyond this repo's own vendor pins_arduino.h
// (no third-party source discusses GPIO13/11/12 specifically), but the
// pins_arduino.h itself is Waveshare's own vendor-supplied file with
// explicit, unambiguous comments ("Onboard QMI8658 IMU", "Def for I2C that
// shares the IMU I2C pins") - treated as a primary vendor source in its
// own right. Exclusion list confirmed, no correction needed.
